<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fruela II of Asturias</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 875–925</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Fruela II of León</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fruela II was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturias">Asturias</a> from 910 and of León from 924 until his death in 925. A son of Alfonso III the Great, he received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturia">Asturias</a> when his father's realm was divided among his sons, and on the death of his brother Ordoño II he took the throne of León, reuniting the inheritance. His short reign was followed by a succession dispute among his nephews and sons.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fruela-ii-of-asturias.jpg" alt="Fruela II of Asturias" width="273" height="314" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fruela2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
